    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "EXHIBIT",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "kinetic",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "SlateCard",
          "props": {
            "headline": "Once a metric becomes the target, it stops measuring what it was designed to measure.",
            "eyebrow": "GOODHART'S LAW",
            "topic": "WHY BENCHMARKS ROT"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "narration_text": "Here's the core failure: once a metric becomes the target teams optimize against, it stops measuring what it was designed to measure. Benchmark saturation makes it worse — models get implicitly trained to exploit a test set's specific patterns, not the underlying capability.",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "actual_duration_s": 17.49,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-12T16:29:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "EXHIBIT",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "RealChipGrid",
          "props": {
            "items": [
              "GPT-3: ~43%",
              "GPT-4: 86.4%"
            ],
            "cols": 2,
            "caption": "MMLU stopped discriminating between systems in about three years"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "narration_text": "MMLU was designed as a hard, expert-level test. GPT-3 scored about forty-three percent, nowhere near the ninety percent human-expert baseline. By 2023, GPT-4 hit eighty-six point four percent. The benchmark stopped discriminating between systems in about three years.",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "actual_duration_s": 20.54,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-12T16:29:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "EXHIBIT",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "kinetic",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "SlateCard",
          "props": {
            "headline": "LLMs don't break. They drift — gradually, silently, without anyone gaming the test.",
            "eyebrow": "THE QUIETER FAILURE",
            "topic": "MODEL DRIFT"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "narration_text": "There's a quieter failure too. LLMs don't break, they drift — behavior changes gradually over time, so a metric well-calibrated at launch can silently stop tracking reality, even without anyone gaming the test.",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.82,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-12T16:29:26"
      }
    },
